The platform should support extensive conversations and long outputs within the real limits of the selected provider.

Do not promise unlimited context or unlimited token generation.

Implement:

- Provider-specific context-window handling.
- Configurable output budgets.
- Streaming long responses.
- Context-aware conversation summaries.
- Retrieval of relevant prior messages.
- Document chunking based on structure.
- Token-aware batching.
- Duplicate-request suppression.
- Caching of reusable outputs.
- Detection of response truncation.
- Continuation from incomplete sections.
- Resumable background jobs.
- Structured intermediate results.

Preserve the important parts of long workflows, including original questions, option lists, equations, code, constraints, units, citations and page references.

When a response is too long, split it at meaningful boundaries and continue from the last complete section.

Do not silently stop after a partial answer or claim that a document has been fully processed when it has not.

Use retrieval and structured storage instead of repeatedly sending every uploaded document into each model request.

Allow the user to choose between concise, standard and highly detailed responses. Preserve completeness when the task explicitly requires every question, option, calculation or section.

Display actual usage data only when it is available. Clearly distinguish reported usage from estimates.

