Potential components include Docling, suitable OCR engines, PDF parsing libraries and compatible vision APIs. Select appropriate tools after checking their current support and deployment requirements.

## Required processing workflow

1. Validate the uploaded file.
2. Extract text and document structure.
3. Identify scanned pages or extraction failures.
4. Apply OCR or visual processing where needed and available.
5. Preserve page numbers, headings and question numbering.
6. Detect question boundaries and answer options.
7. Store source content in a structured representation.
8. Allow inspection of uncertain extraction results.
9. Answer questions using the relevant source material.
10. Save completed work for reuse.

For multiple-choice questions, preserve the complete original question and all available options in their original order.

Provide correct answers, detailed explanations, equations, substitutions, units and page references where available.

For diagrams or corrupted content, flag uncertainty instead of inventing missing information.

Track completed, failed and unresolved questions separately.

